caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/ViewPlacement
title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/tags/view-placement

! Summary
Register a view placement entry for a tiddler type — the entry joins the ''View placement'' settings tab, and the two core ViewTemplate hooks start rendering your panel for that type.

! Detail
Tag a tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/ViewPlacement`:

```
title: $:/plugins/your-plugin/ui/view-placement/note
tags: $:/tags/hypergsd/ViewPlacement
caption: {{$:/language/YourPlugin/Settings/Position/Note}}
hgsd-config: Note
hgsd-default: bottom
hgsd-type-tag: $:/GSD/Note
list: $:/plugins/your-plugin/ui/ViewTemplate/view-body-note
```

* `caption` — the row label in the settings (a lingo transclusion, the core PageControls convention).
* `hgsd-config` — the leaf name under `$:/config/hypergsd/Placement/` holding the saved side (`top` or `bottom`).
* `hgsd-default` — the side assumed while that config is unset; the default-side radio shows as selected.
* `hgsd-type-tag` — the GSD type tag your view renders on; the hooks only render the member when the viewed tiddler carries this tag.
* `list` — body templates in transclusion order (the core convention: listed titles, space-separated). Ship one per member where possible; the shipped project member is the only one listing two bodies.

The hooks (`$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/ui/ViewTemplate/view-body-top` / `view-body-bottom`) loop the tag list per view render: matching members whose resolved side equals the hook's side transclude their `list`. Nothing else names your plugin — an absent sub-plugin is simply a shorter tag list, and the hooks stay inert.

Each body self-gates on its own applicability when needed: the shipped `view-body`, for instance, renders for actions, projects and references but not contacts, so the contact member's `list` carries only the contacts body.

! Best Practice
Keep `hgsd-config` leaf names unique — two members sharing a leaf would write the same config tiddler from two radio pairs.